\" rel=\"noopener\"><br><br><br>ISI Group<\/a><\/h2>\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-41c1c8b e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"41c1c8b\" data-element_type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1836703 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"1836703\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>From humble beginnings as a small, family-run business, ISI Group is one of Cambodia&#8217;s most respected, successful and diversified corporations. With more than 20 years\u2019 experience, our companies lead markets across the building, construction and technology sectors. ISI&#8217;s CSR programs promote positive social change through four key areas: Education, Healthcare, Sports and Housing.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-bd73731 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"bd73731\" data-element_type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-867ce92 elementor-widget elementor-widget-spacer\" data-id=\"867ce92\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"spacer.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-spacer\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-spacer-inner\"><\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>The seminar on shading devices simulating modern architecture in Phnom Penh Green Building: Digitalization in the era of Industrial Revolution 4.0 The Department of Architecture and Interior Design develops human resources with innovation, creativity, and sustainability in the fields of architecture and interior design, aligning with the Industrial Revolution 4.0 era. The program structure is diverse, practical, and hands-on, providing students with the necessary blend of general, oriented, core, and elective courses. The programs also include architectural design studios, project-based internships, industrial placements, and graduation projects. VISION To produce competent and capable human resources in the field of Architecture by promoting integrity, entrepreneurship, innovation, sustainability, and creativity for the industry&#8217;s current needs and future development. MISSION Produce competent architects and interior designers: Be a top university in Cambodia for producing employable graduates who can solve industry challenges within the context of social needs, cultural trends, and climate variability. Provide the best quality of education and learning environment: Foster learning in a productive environment with a constantly updated curriculum, bridging the gap between university and industry requirements by associating students with industrial work (internships) and practical theory. Instill integrity and an entrepreneurial mindset: Prepare students with an entrepreneurial mindset, humanity, and strong interpersonal skills. Impart a research centre: Focus on research in the sustainable built environment. VALUE Professionalism, Entrepreneurialism, Integrity and Innovation, Sustainability. STRUCTURE AND FOCUS The four-year academic is contributed to: \u00a0 \u00a0Design Representation \u00a0 \u00a0History and Theory of Architecture and Interior Design \u00a0 \u00a0Digital Technologies \u00a0 \u00a0Materials and Construction \u00a0 \u00a0Interior Architecture 6.\u00a0 \u00a0Environmental and Sustainable Design 7.\u00a0 \u00a0Building Service and Science 8.\u00a0 \u00a0Planning and Management 9.\u00a0 \u00a0Research and Graduate Project 10. Internship and Industrial Placement CURRICULUM OVERVIEW The 4-Year Bachelor&#8217;s\u00a0 Degree program contains 156 credits combining from 106 credits of coursework, 48 credits of internship and 2 credits of Industrial Placement Report. The courses are divided into three categories, including Common Courses, Specialized Courses, and Elective Courses. No. Course Number of Courses Hours Credit 1 Common courses 11 330 22 2 Specialized courses 21 1,260 60 3 Elective courses 9 360 24 4 \u2013 9 internships (1st, 2nd and 3rd year) \u2013 3 full-time internships\/ Industrial Placements in the 4th year at the industry = 30 credits* 12 2,160 48 5 Industrial placement for whole 4th year and thesis defence &#8212; &#8212; 2 Bachelor of Architecture Architecture has been defined diversely throughout history, and its practice has always been shaped by the advancement of innovative technology. Technology, particularly Artificial Intelligence (AI), has been dominating every aspect of our built environment. CamTech\u2019s Architecture Program is designed to equip students with the skills to use technology ethically, and its core is the smart Design Studio, which encourages students to have an in-depth understanding of building structures and critical issues in architectural design. Students will be able to immerse themselves in new, cutting-edge technology in construction and produce more sustainable buildings locally and internationally. We empower students to use new digital architecture technology such as AI, data analysis, 3D modeling for design, virtual reality, and so on to enable optimal design, sustainable architecture, energy efficiency, a safe environment, and time-saving. CamTech offers a work-integrated learning experience to develop students\u2019 employability, entrepreneurial, and leadership skills. Bachelor of Interior Design\u200b Interior Design at CamTech University focuses on the creation of innovative and exciting, lively interior spaces through the adaptation and spatial arrangement of buildings. The program is designed to equip students with an in-depth understanding of interior space, the relationship between the exterior and interior environment, the use of materials and their techniques for sustainability, and the practical skills and theoretical knowledge required to pursue a career in interior architecture and other related fields. Digital technologies such as augmented and virtual reality (AR &amp; VR) will be utilized to make interior spaces more intuitive in the real world before they are constructed. We empower students to use new digital architecture technology such as AI, data analysis, 3D modeling for design, virtual reality, and so on to enable optimal design, sustainable architecture, energy efficiency, a safe environment, and time-saving. CamTech offers a work-integrated learning experience to ensure students\u2019 employability, entrepreneurial, and leadership skills. Teaching and Learning Methods The programs offered by the Department of Architecture &amp; Interior Design emphasize hands-on and project-based learning. All core courses are delivered through the following platforms: Instruction in English Direct Instruction Lecture slides &amp; interactive discussions Lecture series, seminars, webinars Indirect Instruction Lectures from visiting professionals Tutorial through videos Independent Study Research, presentations, and feedback on relevant topics Group discussions on assignments Practical studies Quiz Reflections at the end of each unit Project-based learning in the Design Studio (including checks, discussions, and feedback) Field visits Slide presentations, course materials, assignments, and the final project are uploaded and assigned in Google Classroom. COLLABORATIVE LEARNING The Department of Architecture and Interior Design encourages collaborative learning, enabling students to work hands-on with various industry experts and through diverse channels for maximum exposure and guidance (focusing on real-world issues). Exchange Program: Opportunities for short-term exchange programs with our academic partners.\u00a0 Research and Publication: Promoting research activities with faculty members and partners. Community and Society Involvement: Attending Green Day, Culture Day, Charity Day, and Environmental Day.\u00a0 Non-Profit Organizations: Collaborative work with non-governmental organizations, contributing to design solution proposals and transforming neighborhoods. Government Agencies: Working with local authorities on various scales, from small installations to urban planning.\u00a0 Industry: Inviting industry guests and practitioners.\u00a0 Job prospects in Architecture and Interior Design: Architect\/Architectural Designer Landsc ape Designer\/Green Architect Architectural Entrepreneur\/Freelancer Architecture and Interior Consultant Researcher in Architectural Praxis Architectural Technologist Interior and Spatial Designer Furniture\/Textile Designer Governor officer Others. Our People Mr. Chea LyBunseang Head of Architecture and Interior Design Mr. Virak Roeun \u00a0Lecturer of Architecture and Interior Design Mr. Nath Kananda \u00a0Lecturer of Architecture and Interior Design Mr. Sonito Pong Lecturer of Architecture Our Industrial Partner Mega Asset Management Established in 2008, Mega Asset Management Co., Ltd is a consultancy company in Cambodia, specialized in real estate development. It manages over commercial and residential [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":7,"featured_media":0,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-25306","page","type-page","status-publish","hentry","post-no-thumbnail"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/25306","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collec